-- title:
--   Finite type of the two Igusa chart algebras over ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number that is nonzero and let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose reduced denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F$ for the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, an extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ containing the modular function $j$ as the element `jFull N`. For a subset $S \subseteq F$, `chartAlg N ℓ S` is the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ formed by the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[S]$ generated by $S$, i.e. the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[S]$ in $F$; the two charts are $B_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, obtained from $S = \{j\}$, and $B_{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ`, obtained from $S = \{j^{-1}\}$. The theorem asserts the conjunction of two statements: $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra of finite type, and $B_{\infty}$ is a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra of finite type; that is, each of the two integral closures is generated as a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra by finitely many elements.
--
--   This is the finiteness-of-integral-closure input for the two affine charts whose gluing along the middle overlap defines the Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) as a pushout of spectra; it supplies the finite-type hypotheses needed for the scheme-theoretic properties of that construction. The proof draws on the transcendence of $j$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, the facts that $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ is a principal ideal ring with fraction field $\mathbb{Q}$, and the finiteness of $F$ over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$.
